# ---- PR create ladder + url reconcile (optional — all defaults are on) ----
# BH-848. `gh pr create` is GraphQL; an App installation token's GraphQL budget
# is exhausted long before its REST one, and a create that dies leaves the build
# record with no PR url — invisible to bin/merge-sweep.sh, which walks only
# records whose line 1 says `PR_CREATED https://`.
# PR_CREATE_REST_FALLBACK=0 (or flags/pr-create-rest-fallback-off) puts
# bin/run-build.sh back on the pre-#848 pair of GraphQL rungs, byte for byte:
# `gh pr create`, then `gh pr list --head … --state open` to adopt a PR the head
# already has. It switches off the REST rungs #848 ADDED and nothing else.
# PR_URL_RECONCILE=0 (or flags/pr-url-reconcile-off) stops the hub lane
# bin/pr-url-reconcile.sh before its walk. The other two bound each tick; what a
# cap skips is reported as `unwalked=` in the tick summary, never dropped.
#PR_CREATE_REST_FALLBACK=1
#PR_URL_RECONCILE=1
#PR_URL_RECONCILE_MAX=50
#PR_URL_RECONCILE_DEADLINE_SECS=240
# BH-858. bin/review-rescue.sh's verdict backfill: how many PR_CREATE_FAILED
# records holding a real `VERDICT: APPROVE` get their ledger verdict row written
# per tick. The pass buys nothing (no PR, no review, no gh call) — the cap exists
# so one tick cannot turn into a long worker conversation. What it skips is
# walked on the next tick; nothing is dropped. Non-numeric falls back to 25.
#VERDICT_BACKFILL_MAX=25

